\title{tidyMacro: Structural Vector Autoregressions and Local Projections via 'C++'}
\description{
Estimation and identification of structural vector autoregressions and local projections, with a compiled 'C++' backend. Shocks can be identified by short-run (recursive) restrictions, long-run restrictions following Blanchard and Quah (1989) \url{https://www.jstor.org/stable/1827924}, maximum forecast error variance share following Uhlig (2005) \doi{10.1016/j.jmoneco.2004.05.007}, external instruments (proxy SVAR) following Mertens and Ravn (2013) \doi{10.1257/aer.103.4.1212} and Kaenzig (2021) \doi{10.1257/aer.20190964}, heteroskedasticity across regimes, and sign or narrative sign restrictions. Local projections follow Jorda (2005) \doi{10.1257/0002828053828518} and cover instrumental variables, state-dependent and nonlinear specifications, panel data as in Mian, Sufi and Verner (2017) \doi{10.1093/qje/qjx017}, and the difference-in-differences estimator of Dube, Girardi, Jorda and Taylor (2025) \doi{10.1002/jae.70000}. Inference uses residual, wild and moving-block bootstraps, heteroskedasticity and autocorrelation consistent standard errors, and one-way or two-way cluster-robust standard errors.
}
